<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    A group heading in the notifications list: "TODAY", then "EARLIER".

    A single TextView rather than a container holding one, because unlike the Tasks tab's headers
    (item_task_section_header.xml) there is no count and no rule to lay out beside it — the heading's
    whole job is to name the group underneath.

    PetCare.Notifications.SectionLabel is the app's shared quiet heading — small, upper-cased by the
    style, widely letter-spaced and muted, in the monospace face used for every micro-label in the app
    — set to this screen's own smaller scale, which is a step below the rest of the app because a
    notification list is skimmed rather than read (see the Notifications block in dimens.xml). Quiet on
    purpose either way: the alert cards below are the subject, and a full-sized heading above them
    would compete with the sentences they carry.

    The margins are the group's spacing: a wide gap above separates it from the cards of the previous
    group, a tight one below ties it to its own. A RecyclerView has no gap attribute of its own, so
    spacing between rows is always a margin on the row.

    accessibilityHeading lets TalkBack users jump from one group to the next instead of walking
    through every card.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/alertSectionLabel"
    style="@style/PetCare.Notifications.SectionLabel"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/spacing_md"
    android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/spacing_sm"
    android:accessibilityHeading="true"
    tools:targetApi="p"
    tools:text="Today" />
